110
00:09:14,190 --> 00:09:17,910
Presents an overview with information appropriately selected.

111
00:09:18,590 --> 00:09:24,310
Pay attention to what band 6 has that band 5 doesn't, or

112
00:09:24,310 --> 00:09:28,190
the mistakes band 5 makes that band 6 avoids.

113
00:09:29,350 --> 00:09:33,670
My question is, choose all the correct answers.

114
00:09:34,490 --> 00:09:37,910
A. An overview is a must for band 6+.

115
00:09:38,510 --> 00:09:44,350
B. Listing detail with no clear organisation means a band 5.

116
00:09:45,010 --> 00:09:49,310
C. Bullet points are acceptable for band 6.

117
00:09:49,950 --> 00:09:55,530
D. Having no data is not a big problem as long as the task is addressed.

118
00:09:56,770 --> 00:10:02,010
A is definitely correct, because in band 5 the writer just recounts

119
00:10:02,010 --> 00:10:07,730
detail mechanically with no clear overview, while in band 6 the writer

120
00:10:07,730 --> 00:10:12,050
presents an overview with information appropriately selected.

121
00:10:12,050 --> 00:10:15,250
B is also correct.

122
00:10:15,970 --> 00:10:20,970
Listing detail with no clear organisation, only to achieve band 5.

123
00:10:21,670 --> 00:10:24,090
However, C is not correct.

124
00:10:24,910 --> 00:10:29,610
By band 6, the writing format must be clear and accurate, whereas

125
00:10:29,610 --> 00:10:33,110
band 5 may still be inappropriate in places.

126
00:10:34,330 --> 00:10:39,670
Band 6 writings absolutely should not have bullet points, they must be

127
00:10:39,670 --> 00:10:41,190
in complete paragraphs.

128
00:10:42,850 --> 00:10:46,390
Lastly, isn't the lack of data a big problem?

129
00:10:47,430 --> 00:10:54,310
Well, it's a really, really, really big problem, and mainly found in

130
00:10:54,310 --> 00:10:59,530
band 5 and below, called as no data to support the description.

131
00:11:00,490 --> 00:11:06,190
From band 6, this isn't a problem anymore, therefore this statement is

132
00:11:06,190 --> 00:11:07,410
also incorrect.

133
00:11:08,690 --> 00:11:09,790
Let's continue.

134
00:11:10,750 --> 00:11:19,110
Task achievement band 5 presents but inadequately covers key features or bullet points.

135
00:11:19,730 --> 00:11:22,830
There may be a tendency to focus on details.

136
00:11:23,390 --> 00:11:29,790
Task achievement band 6 presents and adequately highlights key features or

137
00:11:29,790 --> 00:11:35,810
bullet points, but details may be irrelevant, inappropriate or inaccurate.

138
00:11:36,510 --> 00:11:42,270
My question is, choose the correct answer to move from a band

139
00:11:42,270 --> 00:11:45,290
5 to band 6 in task achievement.

140
00:11:46,890 --> 00:11:49,710
A. All features must be mentioned.

141
00:11:50,570 --> 00:11:53,210
B. There should be no error made.

142
00:11:53,970 --> 00:12:00,330
C. Only key features should be presented and highlighted, not every single detail.

143
00:12:01,210 --> 00:12:05,050
At band 6, you hardly make mistakes in option A.

144
00:12:05,450 --> 00:12:10,550
If you describe all features, it's very easy to list out without

145
00:12:10,550 --> 00:12:16,190
selecting the main information, making the mistake of a tendency to focus

146
00:12:16,190 --> 00:12:21,090
on details that is found in band 5 and below, so this

147
00:12:21,090 --> 00:12:22,150
option is wrong.

148
00:12:24,660 --> 00:12:28,440
Option B is a bit unlikely, even for higher bands.

149
00:12:29,140 --> 00:12:34,980
Even band 6 clearly states details may be irrelevant, inappropriate or

150
00:12:34,980 --> 00:12:40,320
inaccurate, meaning there's still a problem with selecting information to describe.

151
00:12:40,980 --> 00:12:43,180
This option is also not correct.

152
00:12:44,500 --> 00:12:47,260
So the answer is only C.

153
00:12:47,880 --> 00:12:53,120
To achieve band 6, we need to provide key features or bullet

154
00:12:53,120 --> 00:12:57,220
points instead of describing all the details in the chart.

155
00:12:58,600 --> 00:13:02,620
Those are the criterion of task achievement for task 1.

156
00:13:03,580 --> 00:13:06,960
Let's move on to the task response for task 2.

157
00:13:07,860 --> 00:13:13,360
Now, please take the next 2 minutes to find the differences between

158
00:13:13,360 --> 00:13:14,120
the two bands.

159
00:13:14,980 --> 00:13:16,880
Task response band 5.

160
00:13:17,780 --> 00:13:19,700
Addresses the task only partially.

161
00:13:20,460 --> 00:13:23,140
The format may be inappropriate in places.

162
00:13:23,880 --> 00:13:28,960
Expresses a position, but the development is not always clear and there

163
00:13:28,960 --> 00:13:30,980
may be no conclusions drawn.

164
00:13:31,720 --> 00:13:37,220
Presents some main ideas, but these are limited and not sufficiently developed.

165
00:13:37,900 --> 00:13:39,680
There may be irrelevant detail.

166
00:13:40,560 --> 00:13:42,240
Task response band 6.

167
00:13:43,080 --> 00:13:47,100
Addresses all parts of the task, although some parts may be more

168
00:13:47,100 --> 00:13:48,460
fully covered than others.

