178
00:14:21,760 --> 00:14:22,480
B.

179
00:14:22,780 --> 00:14:27,460
Main ideas are more adequate and well-developed in band 6 than

180
00:14:27,460 --> 00:14:28,460
in band 5.

181
00:14:29,020 --> 00:14:29,460
C.

182
00:14:30,040 --> 00:14:34,360
There can be irrelevant detail in both band 5 and band 6.

183
00:14:34,860 --> 00:14:35,220
D.

184
00:14:35,620 --> 00:14:38,060
There is no position in band 5.

185
00:14:38,700 --> 00:14:39,060
E.

186
00:14:39,340 --> 00:14:43,260
There are conclusions in band 6 which may not be available in

187
00:14:43,260 --> 00:14:44,100
band 5.

188
00:14:44,820 --> 00:14:45,340
F.

189
00:14:45,800 --> 00:14:49,080
There is no development for the position in band 5.

190
00:14:50,500 --> 00:14:52,720
A is the correct answer.

191
00:14:53,160 --> 00:14:57,360
At band 6, the writer must address all parts of the task.

192
00:14:58,060 --> 00:15:02,000
There may be some ideas that are not fully developed, but nothing

193
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:02,580
